{"name":"Coney Island","hex":"#6d7e7d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Coney Island","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A neighborhood of Brooklyn, New York, known for its boardwalk and amusement parks."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Coney Island hot dog.","A type of restaurant selling Coney Island hot dogs, popular in the northern United States, particularly in Michigan."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Coney_Island"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coney Island","blocks":[{"text":"Coney Island is a neighborhood and entertainment area in the southwestern section of the New York City borough of Brooklyn. The neighborhood is bounded by Brighton Beach to its east, Lower New York Bay to the south and west, and Gravesend to the north and includes the subsection of Sea Gate on its west. The Coney Island peninsula consists of Coney Island proper, Sea Gate, Brighton Beach, and Manhattan Beach. Coney Island was formerly an actual island, the westernmost in the Outer Barrier on the southern shore of Long Island, but in the early 20th century it became connected to the rest of Long Island by land fill."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Coney_Island_beach_and_amusement_parks_%28June_2016%29.jpg/330px-Coney_Island_beach_and_amusement_parks_%28June_2016%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coney_Island"},{"title":"Coney Island (Cincinnati)","blocks":[{"text":"Coney Island was a seasonal amusement park and water park destination on the banks of the Ohio River in Cincinnati, Ohio, located approximately 10 miles (16 km) east of the downtown area adjacent to Riverbend Music Center. One of its signature attractions, the Sunlite Pool, was the largest recirculating pool in North America and one of the largest of its kind in the world. Coney Island first opened as a picnic grove in 1870, and by the turn of the century, the park had added a lineup of popular amusement rides and significantly increased in size."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b1/Coney_Island_Cincinnati_logo.svg/330px-Coney_Island_Cincinnati_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coney_Island_(Cincinnati)"},{"title":"Island","blocks":[{"text":"An island or isle is a piece of land, distinct from a continent, completely surrounded by water. There are continental islands, which were formed by being split from a continent by plate tectonics, and oceanic islands, which have never been part of a continent. Oceanic islands can be formed from volcanic activity, grow into atolls from coral reefs, and form from sediment along shorelines, creating barrier islands. River islands can also form from sediment and debris in rivers. Artificial islands are those made by humans, including small rocky outcroppings built out of lagoons and large-scale land reclamation projects used for development."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg/330px-Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Island"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/ConeyIslandAerial.jpg/500px-ConeyIslandAerial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/ConeyIslandAerial.jpg/1280px-ConeyIslandAerial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/ConeyIslandAerial.jpg/500px-ConeyIslandAerial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aerial view of the Coney Island neighborhood, which occupies the western end of the Coney Island peninsula","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki